Carcassonne New Edition (toys)

&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;

&nbsp;
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Toys
In 2001 the tile-laying game Carcassonne was awarded Game of the Year and has since delighted millions of fans worldwide. During a game, the players create medieval landscapes and populate them with knights, highwaymen, monks and farmers. Who will succeed, by skillfully placing landscape tiles and deploying followers (meeples), in gaining dominance around the southern French city of Carcassonne? The two mini-expansions The River and The Abbot are already included in the base game. Carcassonne V3.0 now in a new design: the cover is fresher, the rules clearer and the tiles even more detailed.
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Warning! Not suitable for children under 3 years. Choking hazard due to small detachable parts.

&nbsp;
&nbsp;

